{"name":"Blackbird","hex":"#3f444c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blackbird","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A common true thrush, Turdus merula, found in woods and gardens over much of Eurasia, and introduced elsewhere.","A variety of New World birds of the family Icteridae (26 species of icterid bird)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To enslave someone, especially through chicanery or force"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blackbird"}],"entries":[{"title":"Icterid","blocks":[{"text":"Icterids or New World blackbirds make up a family, the Icteridae, of small to medium-sized, often colorful, New World passerine birds. The family contains 108 species and is divided into 30 genera. Most species have black as a predominant plumage color, often enlivened by yellow, orange, or red. The species in the family vary widely in size, shape, behavior, and coloration."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Bullock%27s_Oriole.jpg/330px-Bullock%27s_Oriole.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icterid","wikidata":"Q748159"},{"title":"Turdus","blocks":[{"text":"Turdus is a genus of medium-sized mostly insectivorous or omnivorous birds in the wider thrush family, Turdidae. The genus name Turdus is Latin for 'thrush'."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Turdus_viscivorus_Brych_y_coed.jpg/330px-Turdus_viscivorus_Brych_y_coed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turdus","wikidata":"Q115661"},{"title":"Blackbird (Beatles song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Blackbird\" is a song by the English rock band the Beatles from their 1968 double album The Beatles. It was written by Paul McCartney and credited to Lennon–McCartney, and performed as a solo piece by McCartney. When discussing the song, McCartney has said that the lyrics were inspired by hearing the call of a blackbird in Rishikesh, India, and by the civil rights movement in the Southern United States."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/36/Blackbird_sheet_music.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blackbird_(Beatles_song)","wikidata":"Q880719"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Euphagus_cyanocephalus_male_gaping.jpg/500px-Euphagus_cyanocephalus_male_gaping.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Euphagus_cyanocephalus_male_gaping.jpg/500px-Euphagus_cyanocephalus_male_gaping.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Breeding male Brewer's blackbird apparently gaping (see text) in soil","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEuphagus_cyanocephalus_male_gaping.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Yellow-Headed_Blackbird_%22Posing%22_for_the_Camera_%2822727158809%29.jpg/500px-Yellow-Headed_Blackbird_%22Posing%22_for_the_Camera_%2822727158809%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Yellow-Headed_Blackbird_%22Posing%22_for_the_Camera_%2822727158809%29.jpg/1280px-Yellow-Headed_Blackbird_%22Posing%22_for_the_Camera_%2822727158809%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Yellow-Headed_Blackbird_%22Posing%22_for_the_Camera_%2822727158809%29.jpg/500px-Yellow-Headed_Blackbird_%22Posing%22_for_the_Camera_%2822727158809%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYellow-Headed_Blackbird_%22Posing%22_for_the_Camera_(22727158809).jpg"},{"srcset"